    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40-a1">

                <pb facs="0101" n="27" xml:id="pg27"/>

                <head>Viscount Monck to Mr.
                        Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Government House</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Quebec</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 17, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 11th instant, and its enclosures, relative to the
                    movements of the steamer Georgiana, and to other proceedings reported to be on
                    foot in Canada hostile to the United States.</p>
                <p>I have to request that you will inform Mr. Seward that the Canadian government is
                    fully alive to the importance of preventing the formation of any plans hostile
                    to the United States on British soil, and has taken stringent measures to that
                    end, both of a civil and military character.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
